I made a major step this round: semantic subtyping soundness and the `Sub` typing-rule case are now proved.

## Newly proved and compiling

- `E_from_Vsub` — lifts pointwise value-subtyping to the expression relation: if `V τ ⇒ V τ'` pointwise, then `E τ ⇒ E τ'`.
- `V_secsubtype` — full semantic soundness of `secsubtype`:
  - reflexive and transitive subtyping;
  - arrow subtyping with contravariant arguments and covariant results, using `E_from_Vsub`;
  - `TForallSub` and `TLForallSub`;
  - product and sum subtyping;
  - recursive-type subtyping through unfolding;
  - label raising via the new `V_label_mono`.
- `V_label_mono` — the value relation is monotone under raising an observable type label, with the label-monotonicity field added to `TyRel`.
- `obs_case_label_mono` — the observability wrapper is monotone in the label order.
- `fundamental_sub` — the `Sub_typed` case of the fundamental lemma, reducing expression subtyping to `V_secsubtype`.
- Previously added: `V_mono`, `E_mono`, `EnvRel_lookup`, `fundamental_var`, `fundamental_unit`, `fundamental_bool`, `fundamental_nat`, and the any-level base value lemmas.

## Build status

`make` still stops only at the open target:

```
File "./Task.v", line 1428, characters 0-14:
Error: Command not supported (Open proofs remain)
```

No forbidden proof escapes are present; support files and `_CoqProject` are unchanged.

## Remaining work

The remaining typing rules are the compound-expression cases:

- `Lam`/`App`, `LetIn`, `Seq`, `BinOp`, `If`;
- pairs/sums/projections/cases;
- `Alloc`, `Store`, `Load`;
- `TLam`/`TApp`, `TLLam`/`TLApp`;
- `Pack`/`Unpack`, `Fold`/`Unfold`.

These require the operational run decomposition and heap frame lemmas, plus semantic type renaming/substitution for the polymorphic and existential cases. Semantic subtyping, which was one of the central missing pieces, is now complete.

